# Proxy the API through Netlify so the session cookies are FIRST-PARTY.
# Calling Render directly from the Netlify site makes them third-party
# cookies, which iOS Safari / every iOS browser and many Android browsers
# drop — login "succeeds" but the next request is a guest again.
# With these rules leave VITE_API_URL unset (client falls back to /api).
/api/*       https://surplus-store-backend.onrender.com/api/:splat       200
/uploads/*   https://surplus-store-backend.onrender.com/uploads/:splat   200

# Netlify SPA redirect (must stay last)
/*    /index.html   200
